4) ID-card – a personal electronic (magnet) card ensuring access to University 
territory, facilities and buildings as per stipulated access categories, as well as ensuring 
accounting for movements of persons indicated in Annex 1 hereto. 
5) ACS - an access control service, ensuring control over access mode within 
University territory; 
6) ACP - an access control point, ensuring control over entrance/leave and access 
from/to the University territory;  
7) TAMS – targeted access management system;  
8) MA – material assets; 
9) Point – an access point at entrances/exits at non -residential and residential 
premises of the University;  
10) Secured premises – limited access premises due to the specificity of their 
activity performed within the specified premises.      
11) Block manager – an employee of the Entity  who is a materially responsible 
person for the fixed assets and commodity -material assets located in the Block under 
his/her management. 
4. University territory, covered by present Rules, includes residential and non -
residential premises within University Campus, as well as non -residential buildings 
outside University Campus, which are owned by the University. 
5. Secured premises shall include server rooms, precursor warehouses, 
laboratories, archives, ventilation premises (well -holes), elevators, water supply 
rooms, heating rooms, power stations etc. 

2. Authorized bodies 

6. In order to implement present Rules:  
1) working body is a University entity University Service Management 
(hereinafter – Entity); 
2) Control body is University structural division – Campus Security Service 
(hereinafter - CSS). 
7. entity shall perform functions as follows (via CP and ACS as needed): 
1) issuing temporary permits and ID-cards; 
2) withdrawing temporary permits, which are not valid as of the date of 
representation, as well as ID-cards of dismissed University employees; 
3) check visitors` iden tification documents, as well as permits for entering 
University territory; 
4) suspend access of a person/vehicle to University territory in case of 
incorrectly filled permit document until determination of certain circumstances; 
5) perform visual inspection of any cargo transport passing ACP with respect to 
cargo correspondence with accompanying documents; 
6) control over fulfillment of inside mode by persons/vehicles;  
7) maintaining order in building, premises within University and adjacent 
territory, ensuring University safety, property integrity except for personal property of 
students, employees, tenants and visitors;

